# The server's environment, which is one setting. Copy to
# /etc/conwayskingdom/env, fill it in, and make it root-only:
#
#     install -D -m 600 -o root -g root deploy/env.example /etc/conwayskingdom/env
#
# systemd reads it and puts it in the process's environment, so the token never
# appears on a command line, where `ps` would show it to every user on the box.
#
# Generate one:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Empty is no token, and no token means /api is not mounted at all rather than
# mounted and refusing -- the startup log says which. Whoever holds it is the
# operator: there is no second gate. See docs/server.md#the-api.
CK_API_TOKEN=
